Explanation: The sentence in English is ""I visited them and took a photo."" The original sentiment in Hindi is ""I visited them and took a photo."" To change the sentiment to negative, we can replace the positive sentiment with a more neutral one and add a negative word or phrase to convey the same meaning. In this case, we can replace ""I visited them and took a photo"" with ""I visited them and took a negative photo"" or ""I visited them and didn't have a good time."""
